    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>A scandalous dancer in her mortal life, Miriam Caravaggio was Embraced by the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.GaCuLGcjZZjf2EO6]{Toreador} elder Solomon Greene, who saw genius in her movement. Her fascination with the kinship between dance and combat turned her into a lethally graceful fighter, earning her small fame among Kindred. When offered a @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.ZFYurbvAHfaRguYI]{Brujah} or @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.WaQFCEXFzv8YeAgX]{Assamite} bodyguard, Prince Sara Anne Winder chose Miriam instead, and Miriam has since killed two Kuei-jin assassins sent against the Prince.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>For Miriam, every movement is a dance and every fight a performance. She is a consummate professional who can control her growing taste for combat against the Kuei-jin &mdash; for now.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Solomon Greene. Disciplines (as printed): Auspex 4, Celerity 4, Fortitude 4, Potence 2, Presence 2, Protean 2, Obfuscate 1.",
